;; Clojure's AOT level, the suite compiled (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP3, RPS4 (a), RPS16):
;; the classes every test, spec or namespace of bin/clojure-tests --aot's reference
;; (test/arbace-go-aot-results.edn, against upstream's: test/baseline-results.edn, every assertion
;; passing there) that does not pass or does not run falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's
;; format and with the cases written as REAP1's test/clojure/divergences.edn says: "skip NS: why",
;; "skip NS/TEST: why", "fail NS/TEST (fail F, error E)", "error NS/TEST (fail 0, error E)", "error
;; NS: failed to load: ..."; test.generative's "fail spec S", "error load NS". A case's class is
;; the first whose :match finds it. The level's other classes (diffcheck's Clojure pair beside it)
;; are REAP1's test/clojure/divergences-aot.edn; these are to be appended to that file when REAP3
;; merges (its :f2.4-limit class dropped: F2.4 is fixed, RPS6 (a)), and the suite's source of the
;; [:clojure :aot] cell in test/reap/cells.edn read (its :until "REAP3" dropped). :decided :pending:
;; recorded nowhere yet, the user's to decide (the survey's RPS40-RPS49). Read with the Clojure
;; reader.
[
 ;; the suite: namespaces and tests that do not run (the eval level's, the same decisions)
 {:id :out-for-good
  :title "XML (SAX), gen-class, Java serialization, Swing/AWT, classes from jars"
  :kind :design
  :why "out of the Go build for good, at both levels: arbace.xml's SAX, gen-class (and its AOT-compiled examples), ObjectOutputStream, java.desktop (java.awt.Color, java.awt.Point, arbace.inspector's Swing), tools.deps' jars (arbace.repl.deps)"
  :decided "doc/go/B1-PLAN.md D6, \"Not to be done (the user, 2026-10-10)\"; doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, \"The suite's last failures\""
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.(clojure-xml|genclass|genclass\.examples|serialization|repl\.deps): "
          #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/(test-bean|test-dot|test-proxy-non-serializable): "]}
 {:id :fixtures-excluded-upstream
  :title "fixture namespaces upstream's runner excludes"
  :kind :design
  :why "compilation.load-ns and ns-libs-load-later are fixtures their tests load, not test namespaces (upstream's run_test.clj leaves them out)"
  :decided "upstream's src/script/run_test.clj (clojure/clojure 98d735fab02f)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.(compilation\.load-ns|ns-libs-load-later): "]}
 {:id :d6-namespaces-cut
  :title "D6's namespaces not embedded (metadata's listing, java.javadoc)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "metadata lists the vars of arbace.inspector, arbace.xml, arbace.java.browse, javadoc and shell, and java.javadoc's namespace is not in the Go build: embedding them with their JDK classes cut (Swing, SAX, Desktop) makes both run (SL5, half a day); SL5 was not taken for now"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-NOTES.md, \"Amendments (decided 2026-10-10)\": SL5 not taken for now (RPS18)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.(metadata|java\.javadoc): "]}
 {:id :class-files
  :title "class files: the Go build writes and reads none"
  :kind :design
  :why "compile writes no class files and ASM is gone, at the AOT level too (its compiled classes are the program's, translated by j2g): clj-1208 loads a deftype AOT-compiled from compilation.load-ns whose static initializer loads its namespace; test-proxy-method-order reads the proxy's class file with ASM"
  :decided "doc/STANDALONE-SURVEY.md D13; doc/VENDOR-NOTES.md, hand change 23"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/clj-1208: " #"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-method-order: "]}
 {:id :xml-stream
  :title "javax.xml.stream (reflect's invoke-checks-accessibility)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the test reflects over javax.xml.stream's classes, which are not in the Go build's world (java.xml)"
  :decided "RPS5 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md (deferred)"
  :match [#"^skip clojure\.test-clojure\.reflect/invoke-checks-accessibility: "]}
 ;; the suite: tests that fail (at both levels)
 {:id :fiprims
  :title "FIPrims through interfaces definterface makes at run time"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a fn adapted to an interface made at run time: run-time interfaces carry no annotation, and jrt adapts fns to the world's interfaces only; compiled, the fn is one of the program's classes, but the interface (definterface at load) is still made at run time"
  :decided "RPS5 (a), doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md (deferred, after the milestone)"
  :match [#"^(fail|error) clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/(test-invoke-fiprim-rets|test-match-prim-args-only-to-2) "]}
 {:id :proxy-bitset
  :title "a proxy of java.util.BitSet (not one of the Go build's proxy superclasses)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "proxies extend Object, interfaces and a fixed list of non-leaf classes (J2G-SPEC §5.12, §10.4); BitSet is not among them, compiled or evaluated"
  :decided "RPS5 (a): to be fixed in REAP4"
  :match [#"^error clojure\.test-clojure\.java-interop/test-proxy-super "]}
 {:id :q1-evaluated
  :title "code the tests evaluate at run time: the evaluator's fns are boxed (Q1)"
  :kind :design
  :why "primitive-return-decl and incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws evaluate their code at run time (eval-in-temp-ns, load-string), at the AOT level too: the evaluator's fn is one Go type calling invoke, no IFn primitive interface, so no recur-mismatch warning and no \"Cannot coerce long to int\" (the eval level's :q1-boxed-prims)"
  :decided "doc/go/EVAL-PLAN.md, Q1 (a) (the user, 2026-10-09)"
  :match [#"^fail clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/(primitive-return-decl|incorrect-primitive-type-hint-throws) "]}
 ;; the suite: the AOT level's own
 {:id :compiled-trace-lines
  :title "compiled frames' lines: an unboxed field access or method call, field assignments"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "test-compiler-line-numbers: of its sixteen forms the compiled code's stack traces give five another line than the JVM's: an unboxed instance field (instance-field-unboxed) and method (instance-method-unboxed), an instance field's assignment, typed and reflected, and a static final field's (refused by reflection: the frame is Reflector's caller's line); the frames are j2g's Go code's, its lines the Java forms' (J2G-SPEC §4.3), c2j's forms carrying the enclosing form's line where the JVM's emit marks the inner one (the eval level fails seven others, :trace-lines)"
  :decided :pending
  :match [#"^fail clojure\.test-clojure\.compilation/test-compiler-line-numbers "]}
 {:id :fn-fields
  :title "a compiled fn's closed-over values are its code object's fields, not its class's"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "clearing's tests read a :once fn's closed-over fields by reflection (Class.getDeclaredFields of the fn's class) before and after calling it; a compiled fn is a Compiler$AOTFn made at run time around its code class's object (SA141), whose fields hold the closed-over values, so the fn's own class declares none and the fn reads as cleared before its call. The clearing itself is the JVM's (c2j's emitted code clears as ObjExpr.emitLocal): a fix exposes the code object's fields through the fn's class (jrt's Dyn fn classes) or keeps them in the fn"
  :decided :pending
  :match [#"^fail clojure\.test-clojure\.clearing/(test-clearing|test-nested) "]}
]
